<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan buys 54,000 tonnes of U.S. corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys 54,000 tonnes of U.S. corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Members Feed Industry group bought two shipments totalling 54,000 tonnes of U.S. corn at a tender on Tuesday, Taipei traders said.  </p>
<p>Both shipments, each of 27 tonnes, were bought from Trady Grain, traders said.</p>
<p>The Members Feed Industry Group comprises Taiwan's Formosa Oilseed, Fomau Cereal, Morn Sun Feed Mill and Shin Tai Industry.</p>
<p>Details of the tender are as follows:  </p>
<p>		 U.S. Gulf	    Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> 27,000	March 20-April 4   April 5-19	US$140.40</p>
<p> 27,000	March 20-April 4   April 5-19   90.90 US cents/May</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (886-2-5080815)</p>
</text>
